{% doc %}
  blocks/_showcase-stat.liquid — private to `blocks/_showcase-stats.liquid`.

  One proof card: a glyph, a number, and the sentence that says what the number
  counts.

  ## Why this is not the theme's Icon with text block

  That block is a row — glyph beside words — and this is a tile: a centred
  stack inside a bordered box that has to be the same height as the two beside
  it. Getting there from the row block means overriding its direction, its
  alignment, its background and its border, which is four settings a merchant
  has to know to change and one they can get wrong.

  It is also not `blocks/_testimonial-stat.liquid`, which is the same idea in
  `sections/testimonials.liquid` drawn as bare text with no box and no glyph.
  Both stay as they are: a shared block would be one with two shapes and a
  switch, and the switch is the thing that breaks the section that did not
  change.

  ## The glyph is optional and so is its box

  A stat with no icon is a number and a label, which is a perfectly good stat.
  Setting **Icon** to None removes the element rather than leaving an empty
  square where it was, so the card closes up around what is left.

  ## Everything inherits until it is told not to

  The value, the label, the border and the fill all default to blank and take
  their colour from the section around them. A merchant who recolours the
  section recolours the stats with it, and the two that the design does tint —
  the glyph and the border — are the two with their own pickers.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = block.settings

  assign icon_source = s.icon_source | default: 'icon'
  assign icon_size = s.icon_size | default: 28 | plus: 0

  assign has_icon = false
  if icon_source == 'icon' and s.icon != 'none'
    assign has_icon = true
  elsif icon_source == 'image' and s.icon_image != blank
    assign has_icon = true
  endif

  comment
    ---- the frame ----

    The theme's border group, one width rather than four: this is a filled tile,
    and the frame a merchant wants around a filled tile is the whole outline or
    nothing.

    **Fill** is the one addition. A solid line is one colour all the way round;
    the design this block was drawn from lights the top-left corner in the
    accent and lets it fall away to a hairline of white, which no single
    `border-color` can do. The gradient path swaps the border colour for a
    border-box background layer — see the note beside
    `.showcase-stat--gradient-border` in `base.css` for why that is the
    mechanism rather than `border-image`, which cannot follow a corner radius.

    ---- opacity multiplies, it does not replace ----

    `color_modify: 'alpha'` *sets* the channel, so a picked
    `rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04)` came back out at `alpha: 1` — an opaque white
    tile — the moment the slider sat at its default 100%. The slider is a
    proportion of the colour the merchant picked, not a replacement for the
    alpha they picked it with, so the picked alpha is read back with
    `color_extract` and the two are multiplied.

    ---- filters only, never a colour's properties ----

    The multiply is then handed back to `color_modify`, and every colour below
    leaves this file through a colour *filter*. The `.rgb` and `.alpha`
    properties are not used, and every `rgba(…)` built here by string
    concatenation has been taken out.

    `snippets/color-schemes.liquid` does read `.rgb`, but it reads it off
    `settings.color_schemes`, which is a different object from a block's own
    colour setting. Copying that line down here produced `rgba(, 1)` — an
    invalid declaration — and an invalid custom property is not ignored the way
    a bad rule is: it poisons every property that substitutes it. The fill and
    the frame both went, and a tile with no fill and no frame is very hard to
    read back to a missing comma in a colour.

    A blank colour has no alpha channel to read until the scheme resolves in the
    browser, so the colour filters cannot fade it — `color-mix` does the same
    job at paint time instead, which is the fallback every other bordered
    surface in the theme uses.
  endcomment
  assign border_line = s.border_style | default: 'solid'
  assign border_fill = s.border_fill | default: 'gradient'
  assign border_width = 0
  assign border_paint = ''
  assign border_gradient = ''

  if border_line != 'none'
    assign border_width = s.border_width | default: 1 | plus: 0

    if border_fill == 'gradient'
      comment
        A gradient carries its own alpha in each stop, so the opacity slider is
        hidden on this path rather than quietly doing nothing.

        Each stop goes into the string as the colour object itself, which
        renders as whatever CSS colour the picker holds. A colour the merchant
        has cleared is not nil — it is a colour that prints as nothing — so
        `| default:` never fires for it and the stop would go out as
        `linear-gradient(135deg,  0%, …)`. Hence the blank test and a literal
        fallback: an `if` rather than a `default` filter, because a blank test
        is what matches what an empty colour actually is.
      endcomment
      assign gradient_angle = s.border_gradient_angle | default: 135 | plus: 0
      assign gradient_midpoint = s.border_gradient_midpoint | default: 48 | plus: 0

      assign gradient_start = 'rgba(3, 210, 111, 0.4)'
      if s.border_gradient_start != blank
        assign gradient_start = s.border_gradient_start
      endif

      assign gradient_end = 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1)'
      if s.border_gradient_end != blank
        assign gradient_end = s.border_gradient_end
      endif

      assign border_gradient = 'linear-gradient(' | append: gradient_angle | append: 'deg, '
      assign border_gradient = border_gradient | append: gradient_start | append: ' 0%, '
      assign border_gradient = border_gradient | append: gradient_end | append: ' '
      assign border_gradient = border_gradient | append: gradient_midpoint | append: '%, '
      assign border_gradient = border_gradient | append: gradient_end | append: ' 100%)'
    else
      assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
      if s.border_color == blank
        assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
      else
        assign border_picked = s.border_color | color_extract: 'alpha'
        assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0 | times: border_picked
        assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
      endif
    endif
  endif

  assign background_paint = ''
  if s.background_color != blank
    assign background_percent = s.background_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    assign background_picked = s.background_color | color_extract: 'alpha'
    assign background_alpha = background_percent | divided_by: 100.0 | times: background_picked
    assign background_paint = s.background_color | color_modify: 'alpha', background_alpha
  endif

  assign radius = s.border_radius | default: 24 | plus: 0
  assign radius_mobile = s.border_radius_mobile | default: radius | plus: 0
-%}

{%- capture stat_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', block: s, declarations: true -%}
  --sv-stat-gap: {{ s.gap | default: 16 | plus: 0 }}px;
  --sv-stat-icon-gap: {{ s.icon_gap | default: 16 | plus: 0 }}px;
  --sv-stat-value-size: {{ s.value_size | default: 22 | plus: 0 }}px;
  --sv-stat-label-size: {{ s.label_size | default: 15 | plus: 0 }}px;
  --sv-stat-radius: {{ radius }}px;
  --sv-stat-radius-mobile: {{ radius_mobile }}px;
  {%- if border_width > 0 -%}
    --sv-stat-border-width: {{ border_width }}px;
    {%- if border_gradient != '' -%}
      --sv-stat-border-image: {{ border_gradient }};
    {%- else -%}
      --sv-stat-border-style: {{ border_line }};
      --sv-stat-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if background_paint != '' -%}
    --sv-stat-background: {{ background_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.icon_color != blank -%}
    --sv-stat-icon-color: {{ s.icon_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.value_color != blank -%}
    --sv-stat-value-color: {{ s.value_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.label_color != blank -%}
    --sv-stat-label-color: {{ s.label_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="showcase-stat{% if border_gradient != blank %} showcase-stat--gradient-border{% endif %}"
  data-block-spacing
  style="{{ stat_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- if has_icon -%}
    <span class="showcase-stat__icon">
      {%- if icon_source == 'image' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          A merchant's own mark, so it keeps its alt text: an uploaded glyph is
          often a certification badge, and "B Corp" is content in a way a star
          outline is not.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {% render 'image',
           image: s.icon_image,
           alt: s.icon_image_alt,
           ratio: '1-1',
           class: 'showcase-stat__icon-image',
           sizes: '64px' %}
      {%- else -%}
        {% render 'icon', icon: s.icon, size: icon_size %}
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if s.value != blank -%}
    <span class="showcase-stat__value">{{ s.value | escape }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if s.label != blank -%}
    <span class="showcase-stat__label">{{ s.label | escape }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  Every setting below is a control a merchant reaches in the editor, and the
  schema is one element's styling surface: splitting it to get under Theme
  Check's count of 40 would split the thing the settings style.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% # theme-check-disable ExcessiveSettingsCount %}
{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.name",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "value",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_stat.settings.value.label",
      "default": "300K+"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_stat.settings.label.label",
      "default": "Happy customers"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "icon_source",
      "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_source.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.options.none" },
        { "value": "icon", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_source.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "image", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_source.options__3.label" }
      ],
      "default": "icon"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "icon",
      "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "star", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "check", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "heart", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "tag", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__4.label" },
        { "value": "truck", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__5.label" },
        { "value": "refresh", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__6.label" },
        { "value": "lock", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__7.label" },
        { "value": "clock", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__8.label" },
        { "value": "location", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__9.label" },
        { "value": "mail", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__10.label" },
        { "value": "note", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__11.label" },
        { "value": "info", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__12.label" },
        { "value": "chat", "label": "t:blocks.feature_icon.settings.icon.options__13.label" },
        { "value": "phone", "label": "t:blocks.feature_icon.settings.icon.options__14.label" },
        { "value": "leaf", "label": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.icon.options__17.label" },
        { "value": "account", "label": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.icon.options__18.label" },
        { "value": "bolt", "label": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.icon.options__19.label" },
        { "value": "pulse", "label": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.icon.options__20.label" }
      ],
      "default": "star",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source == 'icon' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "icon_image",
      "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_image.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_image.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "icon_image_alt",
      "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_image_alt.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_image_alt.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:shared.appearance.header"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "icon_size",
      "label": "t:shared.icon_size.custom.label",
      "min": 14,
      "max": 64,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 28,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "icon_color",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.icon_color.label",
      "default": "#03D26F",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source == 'icon' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "icon_gap",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.icon_gap.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 16,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "value_size",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_stat.settings.value_size.label",
      "min": 14,
      "max": 48,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 22
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "value_color",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_stat.settings.value_color.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.testimonial_stat.settings.value_color.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "label_size",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_stat.settings.label_size.label",
      "min": 10,
      "max": 24,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 15
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "label_color",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_stat.settings.label_color.label"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap",
      "label": "t:blocks.testimonial_stat.settings.gap.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 32,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 16
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "t:shared.background.color.label",
      "default": "rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04)"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "background_opacity",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.background_opacity.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "border_style",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_style.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.options.none" },
        { "value": "solid", "label": "t:shared.options.solid" },
        { "value": "dashed", "label": "t:shared.options.dashed" },
        { "value": "dotted", "label": "t:shared.border.style.options__3.label" }
      ],
      "default": "solid"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_width",
      "label": "t:shared.border.thickness.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 6,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 1,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "border_fill",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.border_fill.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.border_fill.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "solid", "label": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.border_fill.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "gradient", "label": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.border_fill.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "gradient",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_opacity",
      "label": "t:shared.border.opacity.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 30,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' and block.settings.border_fill == 'solid' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "border_color",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_color.label",
      "default": "#03D26F",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' and block.settings.border_fill == 'solid' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "border_gradient_start",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.border_gradient_start.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.border_gradient_start.info",
      "default": "rgba(3, 210, 111, 0.4)",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' and block.settings.border_fill == 'gradient' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "border_gradient_end",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.border_gradient_end.label",
      "default": "rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1)",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' and block.settings.border_fill == 'gradient' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_gradient_midpoint",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.border_gradient_midpoint.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.border_gradient_midpoint.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 48,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' and block.settings.border_fill == 'gradient' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_gradient_angle",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.border_gradient_angle.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.border_gradient_angle.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 360,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "deg",
      "default": 135,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' and block.settings.border_fill == 'gradient' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_radius",
      "label": "t:shared.corner_radius.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 48,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_radius_mobile",
      "label": "t:blocks.showcase_stat.settings.border_radius_mobile.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 48,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 20
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:shared.spacing.block_header"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "padding_device",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "desktop", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "mobile", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "desktop"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_top.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 20,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_bottom.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 20,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_left",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_left.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 21,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_right",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_right.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 21,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_top.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 18,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_bottom.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 18,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_left_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_left.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 18,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_right_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_right.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 18,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
